<title>UK: ONS says annual rise in RPI mainly due to housing.</title>
<headline>ONS says annual rise in RPI mainly due to housing.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Office for National Statistics said the annual rise in RPI in May was largely due to housing costs. &quot;There was a major upward effect from the cost of housing rising in May, compounded by the last year's cut in the average mortgage lending rate falling out of the 12-month comparison,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>The all-items index rose 2.6 percent in the year to May compared with 2.4 percent in the year to April.</p>
</text>
